# Copy this file to .env.dev (same directory) to have dev-local.sh /
# launch-isconl-local.sh / launch-isconl-local.ps1 auto-load it on every
# "one command" launch, instead of exporting env vars by hand each
# session. .env.dev is git-ignored -- never commit real values, and this
# file itself must never carry the flags below set to anything but a
# comment.
#
#   cp scripts/.env.dev.example scripts/.env.dev
#
# ISCONL_DEV_NO_AUTH (BS26090501): skips the PIN/TOTP/token wall on every
# engine so curl/scripted API inspection (or just not wanting to sign in
# for local click-testing) works without a live authenticated browser.
# Loopback-gated (every engine refuses to bind at all if this is set and
# its own BIND isn't 127.0.0.1/::1/localhost) and audit-logged
# (auditLog 'dev_auth_bypass' on every bypassed check) regardless of how
# it gets set -- see dev-local.sh's own header for the full safety model.
# ISCONL_DEV_NO_AUTH=1
#
# VAULT_BACKUP_INTERVAL_MS (PI26091101 / FI26091203): how often vault's
# backup loop pushes a generation into the shared OneDrive backup history
# (Sconl/Core/Apex/Vault/vault-backups/vault). Local dev machines must NOT
# push -- only the OCI VM does -- because a near-empty/stale local DB has
# already polluted that shared history once (PI26091001). Both launchers
# already default this to 0 when unset, so you do not need to set it here;
# it is documented so the behaviour is discoverable rather than folklore.
# Set it to a real interval ONLY if you deliberately want to exercise
# backup-loop behaviour locally, and expect real generations to land in
# the shared history if you do.
# VAULT_BACKUP_INTERVAL_MS=0
